id: pm-rlm-tc1023
title: "Make the 2026.10.23 pm toolchain bump pass: regenerate the changelog with the new Closed section"
description: "Continue the existing Dependabot PR changes, preserving valid work and diagnosing failures from full CI job logs. Run the complete package gate, regenerate tracked outputs, and push only to existing Dependabot branches. Never merge or close this item."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-26T18:13:29.796Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T22:08:20.770Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: The existing Dependabot branch contains the verified fix and package tracker evidence; tracked generated outputs match the toolchain; exact-head CI results are recorded
comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T18:14:16.684Z",codex-agent,"Cause: the full failing CI job passes its tests and coverage, then fails changelog:check because pm-changelog 2026.10.23 adds a Closed section. The nested broken fixture is an intentional coverage-gate self-test. Preserve the changelog regeneration. An uncommitted generic lock-conflict retry wrapper from the interrupted investigation was set aside: it is not justified by the CI failure and could hide an upstream defect. Validate the unchanged production code before considering lock-recovery follow-up work."
  "2026-10-26T18:17:26.704Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed upstream SDK recovery regression in 2026.10.23. The Node 26 CI test SIGKILL during root write leaves the previous budget and transcript intact fails with lock_conflict, reason lock_owner_dead, after roughly 3040 ms. Node 22 reaches only the separate changelog drift. A deterministic minimal SDK repro confirms that the commit fence leaves a cleanup gate that outlives the default 3000 ms wait; dead-owner takeover succeeds once the gate expires. The 2026.10.23 changelog documents new fencing (GH-1549), but does not document removal or delay of dead-owner recovery. Do not hide this behind package retries, longer test waits, skipped tests, or lowered coverage.\n\nMinimal reproduction, run as a module in a package with SDK 2026.10.23 installed:\n```js\nimport { mkdtempSync, writeFileSync, rmSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\nimport { fork } from 'node:child_process';\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\nimport { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\nimport { createRequire } from 'node:module';\nconst require = createRequire(join(process.cwd(), 'package.json'));\nconst sdkUrl = pathToFileURL(require.resolve('@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk')).href;\nconst { acquireLockLease, isPmCliExpectedError } = await import(sdkUrl);\nconst root = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'pm-fence-repro-'));\nconst childPath = join(root, 'writer.mjs');\nwriteFileSync(childPath, `\nconst { acquireLockLease } = await import(${JSON.stringify(sdkUrl)});\nconst lease = await acquireLockLease(${JSON.stringify(root)}, 'repro-item', 1, 'writer', false, false, 0);\nawait lease.fence(async () => {\n  setInterval(() => {}, 1000);\n  process.send('fenced');\n  await new Promise(() => {});\n});\n`);\nconst child = fork(childPath, {stdio:['ignore','ignore','inherit','ipc']});\ntry {\n  await new Promise((resolve,reject) => { child.once('message',resolve); child.once('error',reject); child.once('exit',code=>reject(new Error('writer exited '+code))); });\n  const exited = new Promise(resolve => child.once('exit',resolve));\n  child.kill('SIGKILL');\n  await exited;\n  await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 1200));\n  let started = Date.now();\n  try {\n    const lease = await acquireLockLease(root, 'repro-item', 1, 'reader', false, false, 3000);\n    await lease.release();\n    console.log('early takeover succeeded',Date.now()-started);\n  } catch(error) {\n    console.log(JSON.stringify({code:error.code,reason:isPmCliExpectedError(error)?error.context.reason:undefined,elapsed_ms:Date.now()-started}));\n  }\n  await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve,10500));\n  started=Date.now();\n  const lease = await acquireLockLease(root, 'repro-item', 1, 'reader', false, false, 3000);\n  await lease.release();\n  console.log('takeover after gate expiry succeeded',Date.now()-started);\n} finally { child.kill('SIGKILL'); rmSync(root,{recursive:true,force:true}); }\n```\nObserved: {\"code\":\"lock_conflict\",\"reason\":\"lock_owner_dead\",\"elapsed_ms\":3029}; the identical acquisition succeeds after gate expiry. The reproduction sends its readiness message from inside lease.fence and keeps the child alive until SIGKILL. It uses only a synthetic tracker and removes its own scratch directory. Existing production code is preserved; the uncommitted retry wrapper and tests are retained outside the package for review only."
  "2026-10-26T19:06:09.501Z",codex-agent,"Local evaluation crash-boundary matrix completed successfully in 1269416 ms under shared load, preserving unique rows and completed evidence. The complete release gate is still running, so no full-gate pass is claimed. This does not remove the independent deterministic orphaned-fence regression: its minimal default-wait acquisition still reports lock_owner_dead after about 3027 ms. Production ledger code remains unchanged; no retry wrapper or timeout changes were applied."
  "2026-10-26T19:19:25.523Z",codex-agent,"The unchanged local root-write SIGKILL drill passed in 251602 ms. Its large fixture and resumed reads allow the orphaned gate to age out under this host load, so that full-case pass does not establish default-wait recovery. The small SDK-only reproduction removes that timing dependency and still returns lock_owner_dead after about 3027 ms before succeeding after gate expiry. Keep both receipts distinct; the complete npm gate is still pending."
  "2026-10-26T20:24:35.602Z",codex-agent,"Complete source npm release gate finished 377 tests: 374 pass, 3 reported failures including the parent revert-script group, no cancellations or skips. The two failed child cases are evaluation-revert.ts and ledger-storage-revert.ts in the depth-one HEAD clone: regression children exceeded the unchanged 120000 ms bound before an assertion proof was observed. These are unaccepted timing receipts, not successful mutation proofs. All other functional cases, including the large root-write crash drill, passed locally; the small independent SDK orphaned-fence repro still fails default-wait recovery. Bun gate now runs with all available CPUs and unchanged deadlines and thresholds."
  "2026-10-26T20:37:32.972Z",codex-agent,"Existing item pm-rlm-cu already owns loaded-host revert timeout classification and the documented timeout-scale contract, so no duplicate timing issue is created. This task retains the default 120000 ms proof deadlines and records the two timeouts as missing assertion evidence. The SDK orphaned-fence issue remains separate. The current full Bun run is unchanged and still pending."
  "2026-10-26T21:34:30.268Z",codex-agent,"The complete Bun release gate finished 377 tests: 374 pass, 3 reported failures (the two revert child cases and their parent group), zero cancellations and skips. As with npm, evaluation-revert.ts and ledger-storage-revert.ts each hit the unchanged 120000 ms child bound before an assertion proof was observed. Raw coverage is 100% statements, branches, functions and lines; failed proofs mean the release gate is not accepted. Separate npm run audit:prod, npm run pack:dry-run and npm run verify:release-publish-attestation all pass. Packed npm/Bun install acceptance is running separately because the coverage failure short-circuited the release chain. No production source change, retry, threshold or deadline adjustment was made. The independently failing SDK-only orphaned-fence reproduction remains recorded above and in pm-rlm-sdk-dead-fence."
  "2026-10-26T21:57:27.137Z",codex-agent,"Standalone npm run test:install completed: packed Bun consumer passed all SDK/CLI checks; packed npm consumer reached eval-sdk.ts but that child exceeded the unchanged 300000 ms limit. Recorded the distinct acceptance timing follow-up in pm-rlm-packed-timing after duplicate searches. Final npm run build, npm run changelog:full, npm run changelog:check and pm health --strict-exit pass. Both complete release gates remain failed on default-bound revert proofs; the npm install receipt is separately failed. Push the regenerated changelog and complete evidence only, preserving production source and the minimal upstream SDK repro; never mask the orphaned-fence regression."
  "2026-10-26T22:08:19.357Z",codex-agent,"Exact pushed commit 5dd620a08ddf93ccf2a13047340932459ddf0fc4 reproduces the upstream recovery failure in Node 26 CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/actions/runs/40408966320/job/121874051444 . The root-write SIGKILL test reports lock_conflict with reason lock_owner_dead, waited_ms 3013, owner_handoffs 0, while raw four-metric coverage remains 100%. This confirms the SDK-only fence plus SIGKILL reproduction already recorded on pm-rlm-tc1023. Regenerated changelog is preserved and production ledger source remains identical to the dependency bump. This PR remains blocked on upstream default-wait dead-owner recovery; do not add package retries, extend waits, skip the crash test or lower thresholds."
